{"key":"enterprise/T1546.018","id":"T1546.018","name":"Python Startup Hooks","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1546","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may achieve persistence by leveraging Python’s startup mechanisms, including path configuration (`.pth`) files and the `sitecustomize.py` or `usercustomize.py` modules. These files are automatically processed during the initialization of the Python interpreter, allowing for the execution of arbitrary code whenever Python is invoked. Path configuration files are designed to extend Python’s module search paths through the use of import…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/018","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--c5087385-9b7c-4488-9923-d9e370bf08df","source_modified":"2025-10-21T02:35:20.850Z","source_object_version":"1.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0258","name":"Linux Python Startup Hook Persistence via .pth and Customize Files (T1546.018)","url":"https://attack.mitre.